  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.78,
      "end": 2.9,
      "text": "A quick note before we continue."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.6,
      "end": 5.28,
      "text": "The next story discusses suicide."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.33,
      "end": 15.27,
      "text": "In 2025, a journalist named Laura Riley wrote about her 29-year-old daughter, Sophie Rottenburg."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.01,
      "end": 20.69,
      "text": "Sophie had spent months sharing intense personal thoughts—thoughts she hid from the people"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.69,
      "end": 23.91,
      "text": "around her—with a chat GPT persona she named Harry."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.57,
      "end": 29.11,
      "text": "The chatbot consistently responded with warmth and encouraged her to seek professional help."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.11,
      "end": 34.25,
      "text": "But it existed entirely in the digital space, lacking any real-world agency."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.97,
      "end": 36.25,
      "text": "It could not alert her family."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.79,
      "end": 38.35,
      "text": "It could not contact her therapist."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.91,
      "end": 41.61,
      "text": "It could not bring anyone physically into the room with her."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.27,
      "end": 47.53,
      "text": "After Sophie died by suicide, her mother described the chats as a black box."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.03,
      "end": 54.07,
      "text": "The AI offered empathetic words, but those private conversations held crucial details that"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.07,
      "end": 58.87,
      "text": "made it harder for the people around her to understand how serious her distress was,"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.43,
      "end": 60.37,
      "text": "and to intervene."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.15,
      "end": 61.97,
      "text": "This is a protocol—"
    }
  ],
